# TT.OSAG_NOTIFY -- send_test_notification (S-NOTIFY-018, S-NOTIFY-026, S-NOTIFY-028): the one
# public routine with NO exception handler. Four calls: a test SMS (notification type 1), a test
# email (type 2), a type outside 1/2 (fax, 3: the event-type lookup runs, nothing is sent) and a
# nonexistent event type (the STRICT site #10 NO_DATA_FOUND propagates to the caller, P0002 on
# both engines). The routine writes no table on Oracle, so the only comparable output is the
# step table: success or the propagated error code.
#
# SEND PATHS (observed live 2026-10-21, Oracle 23.7 container `mcdb-ora`, no MTA, no network
# ACL): OSAG.OSAG_MSG.send_mail -> UTL_SMTP.OPEN_CONNECTION('localhost', 25) raises ORA-24247
# (network access denied by access control list), logs via plog and RE-RAISES
# (ddl/src/pkgb/osag_osag_msg.sql:60-70) -- the test EMAIL therefore fails out of
# send_test_notification with ORA-24247 (no handler, S-NOTIFY-018). send_sms calls send_mail and
# SWALLOWS (lines 91-94) -- the test SMS "succeeds". The PostgreSQL translation of OSAG_MSG writes
# an osag.msg_outbox row for both (S-MSG-013, DEVIATION(PLATFORM)) and returns normally, so the
# email step is the documented difference in known.diff: Oracle code -24247, PostgreSQL ok.
# The outbox table does not exist on Oracle and is therefore not probed.
#
# ORA_USER=tt: no fixtures; master data only (tt.event_type 101002 with templates 1/2).
ORA_USER=tt
COMMITS=no
COMPARE_MSG=no
DESCRIPTION=send_test_notification SMS ok, email raises ORA-24247 on Oracle (queued on PostgreSQL), fax type no-op, nonexistent event type P0002
